    {
      "id": "ARCH-007",
      "decision": "Router-driven auth with a single reactive auth store; App.vue stops branching on localStorage.",
      "rationale": "Today App.vue reads localStorage in parallel to vue-router and re-syncs via watch(route.path). This breaks deep links (refresh on /student lands on the right component but the nav re-flickers and any consumer of isLoggedIn/user that mounts before the watch fires sees stale data), and a stale user object can persist after token expiry because nothing invalidates it. A single source of truth — vue-router for *where* the user is, and a reactive auth store for *who* they are — eliminates the dual state machine, makes 401 handling possible in one place, and lets meta-driven guards do the role checking instead of v-if soup in App.vue.",
      "affects": [
        "frontend/src/router.ts",
        "frontend/src/App.vue",
        "frontend/src/main.ts",
        "frontend/src/services/auth.ts",
        "frontend/src/components/LoginView.vue"
      ],
      "design_notes": "CREATE `frontend/src/services/auth.ts` exporting a module-level reactive store and a `useAuth()` composable. Public API:\n  - `interface AuthUser { id?: number; username: string; role: 'ADMIN'|'LECTURER'|'STUDENT' }`\n  - `const authState = reactive({ token: string|null, user: AuthUser|null })`  // module singleton\n  - `function useAuth()` returns `{ token, user, isLoggedIn (computed), login(token, user), logout(), hydrateFromStorage() }`\n  - `login(token, user)` writes both to localStorage (keys MUST remain `sql_quiz_token` and `sql_quiz_user` to avoid breaking existing storage) AND sets reactive state.\n  - `logout()` clears both storage keys and reactive state, then the caller (or a one-shot effect) navigates to `/login`.\n  - `hydrateFromStorage()` is called once from `main.ts` BEFORE `app.mount(...)` to seed state from localStorage. This guarantees no flicker on refresh.\n\nROUTER CHANGES (`frontend/src/router.ts`):\n  - Replace `meta.public` and `meta.role` (singular) with `meta.requiresAuth: boolean` (default true) and `meta.allowedRoles?: Role[]` (omit = any authenticated role).\n  - Per-route meta:\n    * `/login`           → `{ requiresAuth: false }`\n    * `/student`         → `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['STUDENT'] }`\n    * `/lecturer`        → `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['ADMIN','LECTURER'] }`\n    * `/admin`           → `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['ADMIN'] }`  (note: today's router lets ADMIN reach any meta.role, preserve this by listing ADMIN explicitly on lecturer-shared routes)\n    * `/practice`        → `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['STUDENT'] }`\n    * `/student/results` → `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['STUDENT'] }`\n    * `/lecturer/practice` → `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['ADMIN','LECTURER'] }`\n  - The existing `/dashboard` route currently uses `component: () => import('./App.vue')` which is wrong (it would mount App inside itself). Keep ONLY the `beforeEnter` redirect logic but switch the component to a tiny `RoleRedirect.vue` (or a `redirect: (to) => ...` function form) that reads `useAuth().user.value` instead of localStorage. Preferred: change `/dashboard` to `{ path: '/dashboard', redirect: () => { const u = useAuth().user.value; return u?.role === 'ADMIN' ? '/admin' : u?.role === 'LECTURER' ? '/lecturer' : u?.role === 'STUDENT' ? '/student' : '/login' } }`. Drop the `component` line.\n  - Single `router.beforeEach((to)) => { ... }` guard:\n    1. If `!to.meta.requiresAuth` (i.e. login) AND `useAuth().isLoggedIn.value` → redirect to `/dashboard` (so a logged-in user typing /login bounces to their home). EXCEPTION: if `to.query.force === '1'` allow through (for token expiry redirects).\n    2. If `to.meta.requiresAuth` AND `!isLoggedIn.value` → `next({ path: '/login', query: { redirect: to.fullPath } })`.\n    3. If `to.meta.allowedRoles` AND user.role NOT IN that list → `next({ name: 'forbidden' })` (see route below) OR fall back to `/dashboard` if `forbidden` isn't desired; choose `forbidden` so the user gets a clear message rather than a silent bounce.\n    4. Else `next()`.\n  - Add a `/403` route `{ path: '/403', name: 'forbidden', component: ForbiddenView, meta: { requiresAuth: false } }`. Keep ForbiddenView minimal (brutalist card, 'Forbidden', 'Return to your home' link that uses `useAuth().user.value?.role` to compute the target).\n\nAPP.VUE CHANGES:\n  - Delete `isLoggedIn`, `user`, `checkAuth`, the `onMounted`, and the `watch(route.path)`.\n  - Replace with `const { user, isLoggedIn, logout: doLogout } = useAuth()`.\n  - Template `v-if=\"isLoggedIn && user\"` becomes `v-if=\"isLoggedIn\"` (user is non-null whenever logged in).\n  - `logout` button handler: `await doLogout(); router.push('/login')`.\n  - `<main class=\"content\"><router-view /></main>` stays; no branching beyond that.\n\nLOGIN VIEW CHANGES (`LoginView.vue`):\n  - After successful POST, call `useAuth().login(data.token, data.user)` INSTEAD of writing localStorage directly. (login() owns the write.)\n  - Then `router.push((route.query.redirect as string) || '/dashboard')` so deep-link round-tripping works.\n\nMAIN.TS CHANGES:\n  - `import { useAuth } from './services/auth'; useAuth().hydrateFromStorage();` BEFORE `app.use(router); app.mount('#app')`.\n\nEDGE CASES (must be handled, tests will check these):\n  - Already-logged-in user hits `/login` directly → bounced to `/dashboard` (which redirects to their role home). Exception: if `?force=1` they reach login (used by expired-token redirect path).\n  - Deep link without auth: `/student/results` typed cold → guard sends to `/login?redirect=/student/results`; after login, LoginView pushes back to redirect target.\n  - Role mismatch: STUDENT typing `/admin` → redirected to `/403`, which offers a link to their role home.\n  - Token expiry: out of scope for this round (P1 — note in backlog); however, the auth store SHOULD be the only writer of localStorage so a future interceptor can call `useAuth().logout()` from one place.\n  - Hard refresh on a protected route while logged in: `hydrateFromStorage()` runs before mount, so `isLoggedIn` is true synchronously when the guard first runs — no flash of /login.\n\nDO NOT introduce Pinia for this round. A module-scoped `reactive()` is sufficient; revisit if state grows.\n\nCLARIFICATION (feedback-loop 2026-05-22): Error routes (not-found, forbidden) are exempt from Rule 1's auto-redirect so that logged-in users still see error pages. Rule 1's exception list must include the route names 'not-found' and 'forbidden' alongside the existing ?force=1 escape hatch; otherwise role-mismatched users redirected to /403 by Rule 3 are immediately bounced to /dashboard, and any logged-in user hitting an unknown URL is bounced away from the 404 page."
    },
