      "id": "ARCH-008",
      "decision": "Extract a reusable StudentMultiSelect.vue component (searchable, keyboard-navigable, with Select All / Select None), in-repo, replacing the inline checkbox list in LecturerView.vue.",
      "rationale": "Correction to the brief: LecturerView.vue does NOT use a comma-separated text input — it already has an inline checkbox list bound to `selectedStudentIds` (lines 675–682) backed by `GET /api/v1/users/students`. The real gap is that the inline list has no search, no keyboard navigation, no select-all/none, no result count summary, and isn't reusable for future use cases (e.g. assigning students to practice sets, group emails). Building a small in-repo component preserves the brutalist monotone aesthetic exactly (a library would drag in styles that fight var(--color-border) and the sharp 2px borders) and avoids adding a runtime dependency for a contained UI concern. Backend endpoint is verified: `GET /api/v1/users/students` (NOT `/users?role=STUDENT` — the brief had that wrong; do not change the backend).",
      "affects": [
        "frontend/src/components/StudentMultiSelect.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/LecturerView.vue"
      ],
      "design_notes": "CREATE `frontend/src/components/StudentMultiSelect.vue` as a controlled component.\n\nPROPS (TypeScript):\n  - `modelValue: number[]`                    // selected student IDs (v-model)\n  - `students: Array<{ id: number; username: string }>`  // caller passes the list; this component does NOT fetch (keeps it pure, lets parent control loading state)\n  - `loading?: boolean`                       // optional, shows a 'Loading students...' state\n  - `placeholder?: string`                    // search input placeholder, default 'Search students...'\n  - `maxHeight?: string`                      // CSS, default '250px' to match current multi-select-box\n\nEMITS:\n  - `update:modelValue` (number[])\n\nBEHAVIOR:\n  - Internal `searchQuery` ref; filtered list is `students.filter(s => s.username.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase()))`. Case-insensitive substring match; do not implement fuzzy matching in this round.\n  - Header row inside the box: search input on the left; `[Select All]` and `[Select None]` text-buttons on the right. 'Select All' operates on the CURRENTLY FILTERED set (intuitive: if a user searches 'sec01', clicking Select All selects only the visible matches and merges with existing selection — do a union, not a replace). 'Select None' clears the FILTERED subset from the selection only (so unrelated selections elsewhere are preserved).\n  - Counter line below header: `'{n} of {total} selected'` where total = `students.length`.\n  - Each row: checkbox + label. The label is clickable (existing pattern).\n  - Keyboard navigation: arrow Up/Down moves a visual focus across rendered (filtered) rows; Space toggles the focused row; Enter does the same as Space; the search input has tabindex 0 and is the natural first focus stop; rows have tabindex -1 and use `@keydown` handlers on a wrapping div with `role=\"listbox\"`. Roving tabindex pattern: a single `focusedIndex` ref drives `:tabindex` per row.\n  - When the filtered list changes, clamp `focusedIndex` to a valid index (or -1 if empty).\n  - Empty state: 'No students match.' when filtered list is empty but `students.length > 0`; 'No students found.' when `students.length === 0` (preserves current wording).\n  - Styling: reuse `.multi-select-box`, `.student-item` look (2px black border, monospace font, sharp corners). Add a `.msel-toolbar` flex row at the top. No new colors.\n\nINTEGRATION IN LecturerView.vue (Assignments tab):\n  - Replace the inline `<div class=\"multi-select-box\">...</div>` block (lines ~674–682) with `<StudentMultiSelect v-model=\"selectedStudentIds\" :students=\"studentsList\" />`.\n  - Keep `fetchStudents()` and the `studentsList` ref on LecturerView — the component remains presentation-only.\n  - The existing label `'Select Students ({{ selectedStudentIds.length }} selected):'` can be simplified or removed since the component shows its own counter; keep the outer `<label>` for the section heading but drop the count (avoid double-counting).\n  - Import path: `import StudentMultiSelect from './StudentMultiSelect.vue'`.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - Root `<div role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Student selector\">`.\n  - Search input has visible label OR `aria-label=\"Search students\"`.\n  - List uses `role=\"listbox\"` with `aria-multiselectable=\"true\"`; each row `role=\"option\"` with `aria-selected` reflecting checkbox state.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE FOR THIS ROUND:\n  - Virtual scrolling. Current rosters are small (<500). Note in backlog if it becomes an issue.\n  - Server-side search.\n  - Async chunked load."
    },
