      "id": "ARCH-012",
      "decision": "Introduce a `useSingleFlight()` composable that wraps any async function and rejects re-entries while one call is in flight. Apply to all primary mutation handlers across LoginView, AdminView, LecturerView, StudentView, PracticeAuthoring, PracticeView, BulkImportStudents.",
      "rationale": "Today every submit handler uses the pattern `loading.value = true; try { ... } finally { loading.value = false }` and the button uses `:disabled=\"loading\"`. This is correct as long as the user doesn't double-click within the microtask before the first click sets `loading=true` (rare but possible), and as long as ALL trigger sites are guarded (some aren't — e.g. LecturerView `createExam` has no `loading` guard at all). A single composable both centralizes the pattern (one place to add telemetry, fix bugs, add backoff later) and closes the race window because the in-flight flag is set synchronously before the wrapped function awaits anything. A composable over an inline pattern is chosen for consistency and because we already have ~14 distinct submit handlers — a copy-paste inline pattern leaks bugs.",
      "affects": [
        "frontend/src/composables/useSingleFlight.ts",
        "frontend/src/components/LoginView.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/AdminView.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/LecturerView.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/StudentView.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/PracticeAuthoring.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/PracticeView.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/BulkImportStudents.vue"
