      "design_notes": "CREATE `frontend/src/composables/useSingleFlight.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { ref, type Ref } from 'vue'\n\nexport interface SingleFlight<Args extends any[], R> {\n  inFlight: Ref<boolean>          // reactive — bind to :disabled\n  run: (...args: Args) => Promise<R | undefined>  // returns undefined on dropped re-entry\n}\n\n/**\n * Wraps an async fn so concurrent calls are dropped while one is in flight.\n * The returned `run` resolves with the original result on the first call, and\n * resolves with `undefined` (without invoking fn) for any call made while the\n * first is still pending. `inFlight` flips synchronously to true on call entry\n * and back to false after the awaited fn settles (success or throw).\n */\nexport function useSingleFlight<Args extends any[], R>(fn: (...args: Args) => Promise<R>): SingleFlight<Args, R> {\n  const inFlight = ref(false)\n  async function run(...args: Args): Promise<R | undefined> {\n    if (inFlight.value) return undefined\n    inFlight.value = true\n    try {\n      return await fn(...args)\n    } finally {\n      inFlight.value = false\n    }\n  }\n  return { inFlight, run }\n}\n```\n\nKEY PROPERTIES (each is testable; regression-tester to cover):\n  - `inFlight` flips synchronously BEFORE the wrapped fn is awaited (no microtask gap).\n  - Re-entry returns a resolved Promise<undefined> rather than throwing — callers can `if (!await submit()) return` if they care, but most won't.\n  - Errors from `fn` propagate to the caller (composable does not swallow); `inFlight` still resets in `finally`.\n  - The wrapped fn keeps `this` semantics intact (we're using arrow functions and free functions here, not methods, so no special handling needed).\n\nINTEGRATION PATTERN (per file). For each handler X that currently looks like:\n\n```ts\nconst loading = ref(false)\nconst doX = async () => { loading.value = true; try { ... } finally { loading.value = false } }\n```\n\nReplace with:\n\n```ts\nconst { inFlight: xLoading, run: doX } = useSingleFlight(async () => { /* original body without the loading dance */ })\n```\n\nThen bind `:disabled=\"xLoading\"` in the template (same prop name pattern). When a single handler currently shares ONE `loading` ref with multiple sibling actions (e.g. LecturerView has `loading` shared between question-save and exam-create paths — verify per file), give each its own SingleFlight wrapper and rename the bindings.\n\nSITES TO CONVERT (audit list — todo-creator to split if too large for one TODO):\n  - LoginView: `handleLogin` -> `useSingleFlight`.\n  - AdminView: `createUser`, `deleteUser`, `saveUser`, `fetchUsers` (fetch is also worth wrapping — prevents double-click on Refresh if added later; but as a no-arg loader it's lower priority — OK to skip).\n  - LecturerView: `createExam`, `saveQuestion`, `assignStudents`, `handleImportSchema`, `toggleExamActive`, `deleteQuestion`. NOT: `fetchScores`, `fetchExams`, `fetchStudents`, `fetchExamQuestions`, `previewCorrectSQL` (preview is an idempotent test; user-driven re-runs are desirable, do not single-flight).\n  - StudentView: `submitAnswer`. NOT `testRun` (re-runnable preview).\n  - PracticeAuthoring: `saveQuestion`, `handleDelete`, `handleResetSandbox`.\n  - PracticeView: `doSubmit`. NOT `doPreview`.\n  - BulkImportStudents: `submitImport`.\n\nNON-GOALS:\n  - No debounce — single-flight is a stricter guarantee than debounce and is what we want for mutations.\n  - No cancellation (AbortController) — only matters for long-running fetches; out of scope.\n  - No queue (so a rapid click during in-flight is dropped silently — DO NOT toast about it, the disabled button is the affordance).\n\nINTERACTION WITH ARCH-011 (form validation): in handlers that ALSO call `form.validateAll()`, do the validation check BEFORE wrapping with `useSingleFlight` would have intercepted it — i.e. validation runs inside the wrapped fn at its top; if validation fails, the wrapped fn returns early WITHOUT throwing, and `inFlight` correctly flips back via `finally`. Example for LoginView:\n\n```ts\nconst { inFlight: loading, run: handleLogin } = useSingleFlight(async () => {\n  error.value = ''\n  if (!form.validateAll()) return\n  // ... fetch ...\n})\n```\n\nINTERACTION WITH ARCH-017 (confirm dialog): the `await useConfirm(...)` step happens INSIDE the wrapped function, so if the user dismisses, the wrapped fn returns early and `inFlight` resets. Do NOT put the confirm prompt outside the wrap; otherwise rapid Delete clicks could queue multiple dialogs.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE:\n  - Wrapping pure read fetches (fetchExams/fetchUsers/etc.) — not a correctness issue and the explicit refresh pattern is fine."
