      "decision": "Introduce two presentational components, `<EmptyState>` and `<Skeleton>`, plus a global `.skeleton` CSS utility. Replace the most confusing pre-load and empty messages: LecturerView tab placeholders, StudentView 'Select a question...' brief, AdminView user table while `listLoading`, StudentResults tables, LecturerView consolidated scores table.",
      "rationale": "Today, pre-load shows either blank space, `Loading...` raw text, or the placeholder content of the next state (e.g. StudentView's 'Select a question to see its brief' is the EMPTY state but reads like a confusing prompt because there's no visual delineation from the data state). A clear separation between (a) loading (skeleton bars), (b) empty (titled card with body), and (c) loaded reduces user uncertainty without introducing icons or imagery (brutalist constraint). Both components are pure presentation — no async behavior — which keeps them trivially testable and reusable everywhere a card, list, or table mounts.",
