      "design_notes": "CREATE `frontend/src/components/EmptyState.vue`:\n\nProps:\n  - `title: string`              // headline, e.g. 'No questions yet'\n  - `body?: string`              // optional secondary text\n  - `compact?: boolean`          // default false; when true uses smaller padding for inline use inside cards\n\nSlots:\n  - default slot (optional)      // for action buttons, e.g. 'Create your first question'\n\nTemplate (single block, no icon):\n```vue\n<template>\n  <div class=\"empty-state\" :class=\"{ 'empty-state--compact': compact }\" role=\"status\">\n    <h3 class=\"empty-state__title\">{{ title }}</h3>\n    <p v-if=\"body\" class=\"empty-state__body\">{{ body }}</p>\n    <div v-if=\"$slots.default\" class=\"empty-state__actions\"><slot /></div>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\nScoped style (matches the brutalist .card aesthetic — thick black border, sharp corners, monospace-leaning typography for the body):\n```css\n.empty-state {\n  border: 2px dashed var(--color-border);   /* dashed distinguishes from real cards */\n  padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-5);\n  text-align: center;\n  background: var(--color-surface);\n  color: var(--color-text);\n}\n.empty-state--compact { padding: var(--space-4); }\n.empty-state__title { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2) 0; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.1rem; }\n.empty-state__body { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85rem; }\n.empty-state__actions { margin-top: var(--space-4); display: flex; gap: var(--space-2); justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n```\n\nThe `role=\"status\"` lets AT users hear the empty message when content changes from loading to empty without rude `role=\"alert\"` interruption.\n\nCREATE `frontend/src/components/Skeleton.vue`:\n\nProps:\n  - `variant?: 'line' | 'block' | 'table-row'`    // default 'line'\n  - `lines?: number`                              // default 3 (only used when variant='line')\n  - `width?: string`                              // CSS, default '100%' (line); used per-line via random-ish widths\n  - `height?: string`                             // CSS, default '14px' (line) | '120px' (block)\n  - `cols?: number`                               // default 4 (only used when variant='table-row')\n  - `rows?: number`                               // default 3 (table-row)\n\nTemplate:\n```vue\n<template>\n  <div class=\"skeleton-wrap\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n    <template v-if=\"variant === 'line'\">\n      <div v-for=\"i in lines\" :key=\"i\" class=\"skeleton skeleton-line\" :style=\"{ width: lineWidth(i), height }\"></div>\n    </template>\n    <div v-else-if=\"variant === 'block'\" class=\"skeleton skeleton-block\" :style=\"{ width, height }\"></div>\n    <table v-else class=\"skeleton-table\">\n      <tbody>\n        <tr v-for=\"r in rows\" :key=\"r\"><td v-for=\"c in cols\" :key=\"c\"><div class=\"skeleton skeleton-cell\"></div></td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n</template>\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n// lineWidth pseudo-randomly varies per index for visual rhythm (deterministic per index)\nfunction lineWidth(i: number): string { return ['100%', '92%', '78%', '88%', '70%'][(i - 1) % 5] }\n</script>\n```\n\nGlobal `.skeleton` utility (ADD to `style.css`, NOT scoped, because it may be reused by `<Skeleton>` and ad-hoc spots):\n```css\n.skeleton {\n  background: var(--color-surface-muted);\n  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);\n  position: relative;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  display: block;\n}\n.skeleton::after {\n  content: '';\n  position: absolute; top: 0; left: -100%; width: 100%; height: 100%;\n  background: linear-gradient(to right, transparent, rgba(0,0,0,0.06), transparent);\n  animation: skel-shimmer 1.2s infinite;\n}\n@keyframes skel-shimmer { from { left: -100%; } to { left: 100%; } }\n.skeleton-line { margin-bottom: 8px; }\n.skeleton-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border: 2px solid var(--color-border); }\n.skeleton-table td { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding: var(--space-2); }\n.skeleton-cell { height: 14px; }\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .skeleton::after { animation: none; } }\n```\n\nNote the `prefers-reduced-motion` carve-out — required for any animated affordance.\n\nINTEGRATION TARGETS (be specific so todo-creator can split):\n\n1. `LecturerView.vue`:\n   - Questions tab pre-exam-select (currently has a `.empty-state` div at L506-508): replace with `<EmptyState title=\"No exam selected\" body=\"Select an exam from the dropdown above to start authoring questions.\" />`.\n   - Questions list when `examQuestions.length === 0` AND `selectedExamId !== null` (currently no UI — it just disappears): render `<EmptyState compact title=\"No questions in this exam yet\" body=\"Use the form above to add the first question.\" />`.\n   - Results tab when `loadingScores`: replace the `<div v-if=\"loadingScores\" class=\"loading-state\">Loading scores...</div>` with `<Skeleton variant=\"table-row\" :rows=\"5\" :cols=\"6\" />`.\n   - Results tab when `!loadingScores && consolidatedScores.length === 0`: render `<EmptyState title=\"No scores yet\" body=\"Once students submit answers, their scores appear here.\" />`.\n   - Exams tab when `exams.length === 0`: render `<EmptyState compact title=\"No exams yet\" body=\"Create your first exam above.\" />`.\n\n2. `StudentView.vue`:\n   - Replace the confusing `<p v-else class=\"muted\">Select a question to see its brief.</p>` at L214 with `<EmptyState compact title=\"No question selected\" body=\"Pick an examination and a question to begin.\" />`. This is the entire raison d'etre of item 4 in the brief.\n\n3. `AdminView.vue`:\n   - Replace `<div v-if=\"listLoading\" class=\"muted\">Loading users...</div>` with `<Skeleton variant=\"table-row\" :rows=\"4\" :cols=\"5\" />`.\n   - When `!listLoading && users.length === 0`: render `<EmptyState title=\"No users yet\" body=\"Create the first account using the form on the left.\" />`.\n\n4. `StudentResults.vue`:\n   - Exam-results table when empty: `<EmptyState title=\"No exam attempts yet\" body=\"Once you submit an exam answer, results appear here.\" />`.\n   - Practice-results table when empty: `<EmptyState title=\"No practice attempts yet\" body=\"Head to the Practice page to start.\" />`.\n   - Pre-fetch state: `<Skeleton variant=\"table-row\" :rows=\"3\" :cols=\"4\" />`.\n\nNON-GOALS:\n  - Do not retrofit `<EmptyState>` into BulkImportStudents (it already has its own copy-driven empty state in the file picker).\n  - Do not skeletonize the SQL editor — it mounts synchronously.\n\nINTERACTION WITH ARCH-015 (sticky headers): when a table is replaced by a skeleton during loading, the sticky header is irrelevant (no scroll). When data arrives, the real `<thead>` mounts and sticky kicks in. No coordination needed beyond NOT removing the `.responsive-table-wrap` wrappers (the skeleton lives ALONGSIDE the real table conditionally, not inside the same wrapper)."
