      "design_notes": "ADD to `frontend/src/style.css` (after the existing `.responsive-table-wrap` block):\n\n```css\n/* --- Sticky table headers (ARCH-015) --- */\n/* Apply to the wrapper to enable vertical scroll AND sticky behavior. */\n.sticky-table-head {\n  max-height: var(--sticky-max-h, 60vh);\n  overflow-y: auto;\n}\n.sticky-table-head thead th {\n  position: sticky;\n  top: 0;\n  background: var(--color-surface-muted);\n  z-index: 1;\n  /* Top + bottom border via box-shadow because border on a sticky element\n     scrolls away with the cell content. */\n  box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 var(--color-border), inset 0 2px 0 var(--color-border);\n}\n@media (max-width: 767.98px) {\n  .sticky-table-head { max-height: var(--sticky-max-h-mobile, 50vh); }\n}\n```\n\nWHY box-shadow rather than border: `position: sticky` keeps the cell in the painted layer separate from the table, and the bottom border drawn on `<th>` will scroll out from under itself when the table body scrolls. `inset box-shadow` replicates the border visually without that bug. The 2px width matches the brutalist border weight.\n\nThe `--sticky-max-h` CSS variable lets a consumer override per-instance: `style=\"--sticky-max-h: 400px\"`. Default 60vh is roomy on desktop and avoids covering the rest of the page; mobile gets 50vh to leave room for the stacked nav.\n\nINTEGRATION:\n  - LecturerView consolidated scores table (Results tab): the wrapper currently is `<div class=\"preview-table-wrap\">`. Change to `<div class=\"preview-table-wrap sticky-table-head\">` (both classes co-exist — preview-table-wrap handles horizontal scroll, sticky-table-head handles vertical + sticky).\n  - LecturerView Questions list table (~L604): same — add `sticky-table-head` to its `.preview-table-wrap` div.\n  - AdminView users table: the `.table-container` div at L161 already has `overflow-x: auto`. Add the `sticky-table-head` class. (Acceptable that `.table-container` is a component-local name — the utility doesn't require any specific wrapper class.)\n  - StudentResults tables (exams overview, practice overview, exam-detail question rows): add `sticky-table-head` to each table's outer wrapper. If a wrapper does not exist, add `<div class=\"sticky-table-head\">` around the table.\n  - ResultTable.vue: its outer wrapper is already `.responsive-table-wrap` (from ARCH-010 / TODO-032). ADD `sticky-table-head` to it. ResultTable also exposes `maxHeight` prop today — leave the prop alone, but if `maxHeight` is bound (StudentView passes max-height=\"320px\"), pass that prop through as `:style=\"{ '--sticky-max-h': maxHeight }\"` on the wrapper. This way the existing per-call height limit also drives the sticky window.\n\nVERIFICATION (manual smoke for validator):\n  - Resize browser so the wrapper engages vertical scroll. Header row remains visible.\n  - Header still shows the full brutalist border treatment.\n  - In mobile breakpoint, header stays sticky as user vertically scrolls a long results list.\n  - When a table is short (no overflow), no visible change.\n\nNON-GOALS:\n  - No horizontal-sticky first column. (Different problem, deferred.)\n  - No scroll-shadow under the header. (Out of scope; the visible 2px border is sufficient.)\n  - No accessibility tradeoff: `position: sticky` is a paint-only effect, AT users continue to navigate the table normally."
