      "decision": "Replace every `window.confirm()` with a Promise-based programmatic `useConfirm()` API backed by a single `<ConfirmDialogHost>` component mounted once at the App.vue root.",
      "rationale": "Native `confirm()` is blocking, browser-themed (breaks the brutalist look), and impossible to style or test. A Promise-returning API (`await useConfirm({ title, body, confirmLabel, danger })`) reads ALMOST identically to the old `if (!confirm('...')) return` line, so call sites change minimally. We mount a single dialog host at the App root and use a module-scoped reactive state object (same pattern as `notification_service.ts`) — no Pinia, no provide/inject, and no per-component dialog instances. A declarative `<ConfirmDialog v-model:open>` API was considered and rejected because it forces every call site to wire a local ref and template block; the programmatic API lets handlers stay handler-shaped.",
      "affects": [
        "frontend/src/services/confirm_service.ts",
        "frontend/src/components/ConfirmDialogHost.vue",
        "frontend/src/App.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/LecturerView.vue",
