      "design_notes": "CREATE `frontend/src/services/confirm_service.ts` (mirrors notification_service.ts):\n\n```ts\nimport { reactive } from 'vue'\n\nexport interface ConfirmOptions {\n  title: string\n  body?: string\n  confirmLabel?: string     // default 'Confirm'\n  cancelLabel?: string      // default 'Cancel'\n  danger?: boolean          // default false — when true, confirm button uses red brutalist styling\n}\n\ninterface PendingConfirm extends ConfirmOptions {\n  id: number\n  resolve: (value: boolean) => void\n}\n\nconst state = reactive<{ current: PendingConfirm | null }>({ current: null })\nlet nextId = 1\n\nexport function useConfirm() {\n  function confirm(opts: ConfirmOptions): Promise<boolean> {\n    return new Promise<boolean>((resolve) => {\n      // If a confirm is already open, reject the previous one (resolve false) to avoid stacking.\n      if (state.current) state.current.resolve(false)\n      state.current = { ...opts, id: nextId++, resolve }\n    })\n  }\n  function _resolveCurrent(value: boolean) {\n    if (!state.current) return\n    const c = state.current\n    state.current = null\n    c.resolve(value)\n  }\n  return { state, confirm, _resolveCurrent }\n}\n```\n\nThe `_resolveCurrent` is internal — consumed only by `ConfirmDialogHost`. Exposing it via the same composable instead of a second export keeps the API surface single-import.\n\nCREATE `frontend/src/components/ConfirmDialogHost.vue`:\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { computed, onMounted, onBeforeUnmount, nextTick, ref, watch } from 'vue'\nimport { useConfirm } from '../services/confirm_service'\n\nconst { state, _resolveCurrent } = useConfirm()\nconst confirmBtnRef = ref<HTMLButtonElement | null>(null)\nconst open = computed(() => state.current !== null)\n\nfunction onCancel() { _resolveCurrent(false) }\nfunction onConfirm() { _resolveCurrent(true) }\n\nfunction onKeydown(e: KeyboardEvent) {\n  if (!open.value) return\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') { e.preventDefault(); onCancel() }\n  if (e.key === 'Enter')  { e.preventDefault(); onConfirm() }\n}\n\nonMounted(() => window.addEventListener('keydown', onKeydown))\nonBeforeUnmount(() => window.removeEventListener('keydown', onKeydown))\n\nwatch(open, async (v) => { if (v) { await nextTick(); confirmBtnRef.value?.focus() } })\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <Teleport to=\"body\">\n    <div v-if=\"open && state.current\" class=\"confirm-backdrop\" @click.self=\"onCancel\" role=\"presentation\">\n      <div class=\"confirm-dialog\" role=\"alertdialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" :aria-labelledby=\"'confirm-title-' + state.current.id\">\n        <h3 :id=\"'confirm-title-' + state.current.id\" class=\"confirm-title\">{{ state.current.title }}</h3>\n        <p v-if=\"state.current.body\" class=\"confirm-body\">{{ state.current.body }}</p>\n        <div class=\"confirm-actions\">\n          <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" @click=\"onCancel\">{{ state.current.cancelLabel || 'Cancel' }}</button>\n          <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" :class=\"state.current.danger ? 'btn-danger' : 'btn-primary'\" ref=\"confirmBtnRef\" @click=\"onConfirm\">\n            {{ state.current.confirmLabel || 'Confirm' }}\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </Teleport>\n</template>\n\n<style scoped>\n.confirm-backdrop {\n  position: fixed; inset: 0;\n  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.5);\n  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n  z-index: 10000; padding: var(--space-4);\n}\n.confirm-dialog {\n  background: var(--color-surface);\n  border: 2px solid var(--color-border);\n  padding: var(--space-5);\n  max-width: 480px; width: 100%;\n}\n.confirm-title { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) 0; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.1rem; }\n.confirm-body  { margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0; color: var(--color-text); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9rem; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n.confirm-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--space-2); justify-content: flex-end; }\n.btn-danger { background: var(--color-danger); color: var(--color-surface); border-color: var(--color-danger); }\n</style>\n```\n\nMOUNT IN App.vue:\n  - Import `ConfirmDialogHost` and place it as a SIBLING of `NotificationToast` near the end of `<template>`. It uses `<Teleport to=\"body\">` so it does not affect layout.\n\nCALL-SITE CONVERSIONS:\n  - `LecturerView.vue:71` `deleteQuestion`:\n    ```ts\n    const { confirm } = useConfirm()\n    const deleteQuestion = async (id: number) => {\n      const ok = await confirm({ title: 'Delete this question?', body: 'This cannot be undone.', confirmLabel: 'Delete', danger: true })\n      if (!ok) return\n      // ... rest of body unchanged ...\n    }\n    ```\n  - `AdminView.vue:66` `deleteUser`: same shape, title 'Delete this user?'.\n  - `PracticeAuthoring.vue:78` `handleDelete`: same shape, title 'Delete this practice question?'.\n  - `PracticeAuthoring.vue:114` `handleResetSandbox`: title 'Reset practice sandbox?', body 'This drops and recreates the sandbox_practice schema. Existing student attempts in the sandbox will be lost.', confirmLabel 'Reset', danger: true.\n\nFOCUS MANAGEMENT (covers a slice of P2 item 15):\n  - On open, focus the confirm button (done in the watcher above). Escape cancels, Enter confirms.\n  - The dialog uses `role=\"alertdialog\"` + `aria-modal=\"true\"`. No focus trap is implemented in this round — escape-to-close + click-out-to-cancel + autofocus on confirm covers 95% of the UX. Full focus trap (cycling Tab) is deferred to a follow-up if needed; if you DO implement it, use the standard 'find first/last focusable' pattern within `.confirm-dialog`.\n\nSTACKING:\n  - The `confirm()` API resolves any prior pending confirm with `false` before opening a new one. Rationale: stacking dialogs is almost always a bug (user clicked Delete twice rapidly); resolving the previous as false matches user intent (cancel) without leaking unresolved promises.\n\nNON-GOALS:\n  - No `prompt()`-style input dialogs in this round.\n  - No animation (brutalist — instant show/hide).\n  - No multi-step wizards.\n\nTESTING (regression-tester):\n  - `useConfirm().confirm(opts)` returns a Promise.\n  - Clicking Confirm resolves true, Cancel resolves false, backdrop click resolves false, Escape resolves false, Enter resolves true.\n  - Opening a second confirm while the first is pending resolves the first with false and replaces it.\n  - Title/body/labels render from opts; `danger: true` toggles `.btn-danger`.\n  - After mount, the confirm button receives focus.\n\nINTERACTION WITH ARCH-012 (single-flight): see ARCH-012 design_notes — confirm calls live INSIDE the wrapped fn so cancellation cleanly resets `inFlight`."
