      "id": "ARCH-018",
      "decision": "Standardize error UX into two channels: (1) fire-and-forget API/mutation errors route through `NotificationToast` via a new `handleApiError(err, ctx?)` helper; (2) form-field-level errors continue to use the inline pattern from ARCH-011. Remove every `error.value = err.message` for mutation errors and replace with `handleApiError(err, { fallback: '...' })`.",
      "rationale": "Two coexisting error UX paths today: most components use `notify(err.message, 'error')` (good), but a few (LecturerView's `fetchStudents`/`fetchExams`, StudentView's `submitAnswer`) push errors into a local `error` ref that is rendered who-knows-where (or not at all). The mixed style hides real failures and confuses users. A single `handleApiError` helper that always emits a toast, normalizes thrown `Error`, raw strings, fetch `Response` instances, and unknowns into a consistent message, removes the cognitive load of writing error handling inline and centralizes the place to add things like Sentry logging later.",
      "affects": [
