      "design_notes": "NotificationToast contract (verified from the file): `useNotifications().notify(message: string, type: 'success'|'error'|'info', duration?: number)`. Toast component is mounted in App.vue (existing). We reuse this surface exclusively for mutation/fetch errors.\n\nCREATE `frontend/src/services/error_handler.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { useNotifications } from './notification_service'\n\nexport interface HandleApiErrorContext {\n  fallback?: string           // default 'Something went wrong.'\n  silent?: boolean            // default false — when true, do NOT emit a toast (rare; useful for background polls)\n  toastDuration?: number      // default 5000\n}\n\n/**\n * Normalize an arbitrary thrown value into a user-facing string and surface it as an error toast.\n * Returns the normalized string so callers may use it for additional logging.\n */\nexport function handleApiError(err: unknown, ctx: HandleApiErrorContext = {}): string {\n  const fallback = ctx.fallback || 'Something went wrong.'\n  let message = fallback\n\n  if (err instanceof Error) {\n    message = err.message || fallback\n  } else if (typeof err === 'string') {\n    message = err || fallback\n  } else if (err && typeof err === 'object' && 'message' in err && typeof (err as any).message === 'string') {\n    message = (err as any).message || fallback\n  } else if (err && typeof err === 'object' && 'error' in err && typeof (err as any).error === 'string') {\n    message = (err as any).error || fallback\n  }\n\n  if (!ctx.silent) {\n    const { notify } = useNotifications()\n    notify(message, 'error', ctx.toastDuration)\n  }\n  return message\n}\n\n/**\n * Helper to convert a non-OK Response into a thrown Error with the best available message.\n * Use as: `if (!res.ok) throw await toApiError(res, 'Failed to save question')`.\n */\nexport async function toApiError(res: Response, fallback: string): Promise<Error> {\n  let body: any = null\n  try { body = await res.json() } catch { /* not JSON */ }\n  const msg = (body && (body.error || body.message)) || `${fallback} (HTTP ${res.status})`\n  return new Error(msg)\n}\n```\n\nWhy two helpers: `toApiError` is for the `if (!res.ok)` branch (we throw, then a single outer catch handles it). `handleApiError` is for the `catch` block.\n\nCALL-SITE CONVERSIONS (mechanical):\n\nBefore:\n```ts\ntry {\n  const res = await fetch(url, opts)\n  if (!res.ok) { const e = await res.json(); throw new Error(e.error || 'Failed to ...') }\n  // success path\n} catch (err: any) {\n  notify(err.message, 'error')\n}\n```\nAfter:\n```ts\ntry {\n  const res = await fetch(url, opts)\n  if (!res.ok) throw await toApiError(res, 'Failed to save the question')\n  // success path\n} catch (err) {\n  handleApiError(err, { fallback: 'Failed to save the question' })\n}\n```\n\nFILES + SPECIFIC SITES:\n\n  - `LecturerView.vue`:\n    * `fetchStudents` catch -> `handleApiError(err, { fallback: 'Failed to load students' })`. Remove the `error.value = err.message` line.\n    * `fetchExams` catch -> same. Remove the `error.value = err.message` line. Also convert the `!response.ok` branch to throw via `toApiError` instead of the current `error.value = errData.error || ...`.\n    * `createExam`, `toggleExamActive`, `assignStudents`, `handleImportSchema`, `saveQuestion`, `deleteQuestion`, `previewCorrectSQL`, `fetchExamQuestions`, `fetchScores`: keep the toast pattern but route through `handleApiError`. Use `toApiError` for non-OK responses (currently each writes a bespoke `errData.error || ...` line).\n    * Delete the unused `error` ref if no `<p v-if=\"error\">` template usage remains (it appears not to be rendered anywhere). Audit and remove dead refs.\n\n  - `StudentView.vue`:\n    * `submitAnswer`: KEEP the local validation lines that set `error.value` for 'Please provide a SQL query.' / 'Please select a question.' — these are form-level validation (item 1's territory) and should remain inline (or be converted to ARCH-011 pattern if/when that lands here, but NOT in this round). The CATCH for the fetch failure currently routes through `notify(err.message, 'error')` — convert to `handleApiError(err, { fallback: 'Failed to submit answer' })`.\n    * `testRun`: same — convert all the `notify(...)` lines that fire on bad HTTP codes to `handleApiError(new Error('Server busy, please try again'), { fallback: ... })` ONLY where they relate to thrown errors. The explicit `notify('Server busy...')` for 503 is fine as-is (it's a user-facing status, not an error normalization).\n  \n  - `AdminView.vue`:\n    * `fetchUsers`, `createUser`, `deleteUser`, `saveUser`: convert each catch to `handleApiError`. Use `toApiError` on the `!res.ok` branches.\n\n  - `PracticeAuthoring.vue`:\n    * `handlePreview`, `saveQuestion`, `handleDelete`, `handleResetSandbox`: same conversion.\n\n  - `PracticeView.vue`:\n    * `loadData`, `doSubmit`, `doPreview`: same conversion. The `notify('Failed to load practice questions.', 'error')` is a hard-coded string already — easy to swap to `handleApiError(err, { fallback: 'Failed to load practice questions.' })`.\n\n  - `BulkImportStudents.vue`:\n    * `submitImport`: same conversion.\n\n  - `StudentResults.vue`:\n    * `fetchExamResults`, `fetchPracticeResults`, `fetchExamDetails` (per file scan): convert each catch.\n\n  - `LoginView.vue`:\n    * KEEP the inline `error` ref render — login is a special case where the error is field-level (invalid credentials apply to the form, not a fire-and-forget mutation). The pattern from ARCH-011 will eventually subsume this. NO CHANGE in this round beyond the ARCH-011 work.\n\nINTERACTION WITH ARCH-011:\n  - 'Inline error refs are okay for form-level validation feedback' — i.e. LoginView's local `error.value = 'Invalid username or password'` stays. ARCH-011's `FieldError` is for field-specific errors; the login server error is form-level (whole-form), so it's neither inline-field NOR a toast. Acceptable.\n\nINTERACTION WITH ARCH-012:\n  - `useSingleFlight` allows fn to throw; `handleApiError` consumes the throw. Pattern remains clean.\n\nINTERACTION WITH ARCH-017:\n  - `useConfirm()` rejects -> no exception thrown; handler simply `return`s on `!ok`. No error path interaction.\n\nNON-GOALS:\n  - No global axios/fetch interceptor in this round. Each call site continues to use `fetch` directly. (When/if an HTTP client is centralized, the interceptor can call `handleApiError` from one place.)\n  - No retry logic.\n  - No error code -> i18n message mapping.\n  - No silencing of expected 401 logout flows (deferred to a future token-expiry interceptor item).\n\nTESTING (regression-tester):\n  - `handleApiError(new Error('boom'))` -> notify called with 'boom', 'error'.\n  - `handleApiError('boom')` -> notify called with 'boom'.\n  - `handleApiError({ error: 'server msg' })` -> notify called with 'server msg'.\n  - `handleApiError(null, { fallback: 'oops' })` -> notify called with 'oops'.\n  - `handleApiError(err, { silent: true })` -> notify NOT called.\n  - `toApiError(new Response('{\"error\":\"x\"}', { status: 400 }), 'fallback')` -> Error with message 'x'.\n  - `toApiError(new Response('not json', { status: 500 }), 'fallback')` -> Error with message 'fallback (HTTP 500)'."
