      "design_notes": "CREATE `frontend/src/composables/useAutosave.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { onBeforeUnmount, watch, type Ref } from 'vue'\n\nexport interface UseAutosaveOptions {\n  debounceMs?: number          // default 600\n  minLength?: number           // default 10 — only save if length >= minLength, otherwise clear\n  storage?: Storage            // default window.localStorage (injectable for tests)\n}\n\nexport interface UseAutosaveReturn {\n  hasDraft: () => boolean      // true if a non-empty draft exists at `key`\n  loadDraft: () => string | null   // returns the stored draft (or null) WITHOUT mutating the ref\n  restoreDraft: () => boolean  // copies draft into the ref; returns true if restored\n  clearDraft: () => void       // removes the draft from storage\n  flush: () => void            // writes current value synchronously (use before manual submit)\n}\n\nexport function useAutosave(\n  key: string,\n  valueRef: Ref<string>,\n  options: UseAutosaveOptions = {}\n): UseAutosaveReturn {\n  const storage = options.storage || (typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.localStorage : null)\n  const debounceMs = options.debounceMs ?? 600\n  const minLength = options.minLength ?? 10\n\n  let timer: number | null = null\n  function write() {\n    if (!storage) return\n    const v = valueRef.value || ''\n    if (v.length < minLength) {\n      storage.removeItem(key)\n    } else {\n      try { storage.setItem(key, v) } catch { /* quota — silently ignore */ }\n    }\n  }\n  function schedule() {\n    if (timer != null) window.clearTimeout(timer)\n    timer = window.setTimeout(() => { write(); timer = null }, debounceMs)\n  }\n  watch(valueRef, schedule)\n  onBeforeUnmount(() => { if (timer != null) { window.clearTimeout(timer); write() } })\n\n  return {\n    hasDraft: () => !!(storage && storage.getItem(key)),\n    loadDraft: () => storage ? storage.getItem(key) : null,\n    restoreDraft: () => {\n      if (!storage) return false\n      const d = storage.getItem(key)\n      if (d == null) return false\n      valueRef.value = d\n      return true\n    },\n    clearDraft: () => { if (storage) storage.removeItem(key) },\n    flush: () => { if (timer != null) { window.clearTimeout(timer); timer = null } write() },\n  }\n}\n```\n\nKEY NAMING CONVENTION (mandatory):\n  - `sql_quiz_draft.<view>.<field>[.<scope>]`\n  - Examples:\n    * LecturerView question requirement, scoped per exam: `sql_quiz_draft.lecturer.questionRequirement.exam-<examId>`\n    * PracticeAuthoring requirement: `sql_quiz_draft.practiceAuthoring.requirement`\n  - Reason: prefix `sql_quiz_` matches the existing `sql_quiz_token` / `sql_quiz_user` namespace and makes future cleanup easy.\n  - Per-exam scoping for the LecturerView field means switching exams does NOT cross-pollute drafts.\n\nRESTORE TRIGGER (deliberate UX choice):\n  - DO NOT auto-restore on mount. The user may have closed the tab on purpose intending a fresh form.\n  - INSTEAD: on mount AND whenever the relevant scope key changes (e.g. user picks a different exam in LecturerView), check `hasDraft()`. If true, show a small inline banner above the textarea:\n    ```vue\n    <div v-if=\"showDraftBanner\" class=\"draft-banner\">\n      A draft from your previous session is available.\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-sm\" @click=\"acceptDraft\">Restore</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-sm\" @click=\"dismissDraft\">Discard</button>\n    </div>\n    ```\n  - `acceptDraft`: `restoreDraft(); showDraftBanner = false`.\n  - `dismissDraft`: `clearDraft(); showDraftBanner = false`.\n  - Style the banner with the existing brutalist palette: 1px dashed black border, monospace font, `var(--color-surface-muted)` background. No new color vars.\n\nCLEAR ON SUCCESSFUL SAVE:\n  - In each save handler (LecturerView `saveQuestion`, PracticeAuthoring `saveQuestion`), call `clearDraft()` inside the SUCCESS branch (NOT in `finally` — we do NOT want to clear on failure).\n\nINTEGRATION IN LecturerView.vue:\n  - Import: `import { useAutosave } from '../composables/useAutosave'`.\n  - At top of `<script setup>`:\n    ```ts\n    const requirementKey = computed(() => `sql_quiz_draft.lecturer.questionRequirement.exam-${question.value.exam_id ?? 'none'}`)\n    const requirementRef = computed({\n      get: () => question.value.requirement,\n      set: (v: string) => { question.value.requirement = v }\n    })\n    // Use a stable string for the key — pass via a watcher because useAutosave wants a static key per call.\n    ```\n  - Because the key is reactive (changes with exam), the cleanest approach is to instantiate `useAutosave` lazily inside a `watchEffect` that re-creates on key change, OR to add a `keyRef?: Ref<string>` option to the composable.\n  - SIMPLER ALTERNATIVE (RECOMMENDED): wrap the textarea + autosave in a small inline subcomponent or just use ONE call with a key that always points to the current exam by reading `question.value.exam_id` inside the watcher. Acceptable since the user can only have one form open at a time. Implementor judgment.\n  - DRAFT BANNER: render above the textarea at L542. Toggle `showDraftBanner` based on `hasDraft()` whenever the working exam changes.\n  - In `saveQuestion` success branch (after `notify` of success and before resetting `question`): call `clearDraft()`.\n\nINTEGRATION IN PracticeAuthoring.vue:\n  - Identical pattern, key `sql_quiz_draft.practiceAuthoring.requirement`. Banner above the requirement textarea (~L204). Clear on success.\n\nSQL EDITOR DECISION (StudentView / PracticeView):\n  - NO autosave. Justification: quiz answers are transient by design and the existing `watch(selectedQuestionId, () => { sqlText.value = '' })` is a feature (clean slate per question). Persisting a half-typed wrong answer across sessions would confuse students and create cheating concerns.\n  - Document this decision in `docs/ui_ux_backlog.md` so a future round knows we deliberately punted.\n\nAUDIT OF OTHER LONG-FORM INPUTS (per file scan):\n  - LecturerView import schema textarea (`importSQL`): SKIP. Pasting a multi-megabyte schema script into localStorage flirts with the ~5MB quota; rare workflow; user explicitly pastes from a file.\n  - StudentView SQL editor: SKIP per above.\n  - PracticeView SQL editor: SKIP per above.\n  - BulkImportStudents: file input only, not textareas.\n  - AdminView: no long-form text inputs.\n\nNON-GOALS:\n  - No multi-tab synchronization via `storage` events.\n  - No conflict resolution (e.g. server-side draft merge).\n  - No encryption — these are non-sensitive question-authoring drafts on the author's own machine.\n\nTESTING (regression-tester):\n  - Composable unit tests using an injected mock Storage:\n    * Writing to the ref schedules a save after `debounceMs`.\n    * Multiple rapid writes coalesce into one storage write.\n    * Values shorter than `minLength` clear the key instead of writing.\n    * `restoreDraft()` mutates the ref and returns true; on missing draft returns false.\n    * `clearDraft()` removes the key.\n    * `flush()` writes synchronously and cancels pending debounce.\n  - Integration test on LecturerView: typing into the requirement textarea, switching exam, switching back -> banner appears; clicking Restore brings text back; clicking Discard clears storage.\n  - Integration test on PracticeAuthoring: save success -> draft cleared."
