      "design_notes": "NEW FILE `frontend/src/composables/useKeyboardShortcut.ts`. Public API:\n```ts\nexport interface ShortcutBinding {\n  combo: string            // e.g. 'Ctrl+Enter', 'Escape', 'Mod+/'\n                           // 'Mod' = Cmd on macOS, Ctrl elsewhere (detect via navigator.platform)\n  handler: (e: KeyboardEvent) => void\n  // If true, fire even when focus is inside <input>, <textarea>, [contenteditable], .cm-editor.\n  // Default false: skip when typing in those elements.\n  whenTyping?: boolean\n  // Optional ref to scope the binding (only fires if e.target is inside el.value). Default: window.\n  scope?: Ref<HTMLElement | null>\n}\nexport function useKeyboardShortcut(bindings: ShortcutBinding | ShortcutBinding[]): void\n```\nImplementation outline: in `onMounted` attach a single `keydown` listener on window; iterate bindings; parse `combo` into `{key, ctrl, shift, alt, meta}`. Skip bindings where `e.target` matches `input, textarea, [contenteditable], .cm-editor *` unless `whenTyping`. Always call `e.preventDefault()` if a binding matches and returns truthy (handler may return false to opt out). Tear down in `onBeforeUnmount`. No external dep.\n\nGOVERNED SHORTCUTS (round 1, narrow scope):\n- `Ctrl+Enter` (whenTyping:true) in StudentView/PracticeView: submit answer. Bound on the SqlEditor wrapper scope so it does not fire on the navbar.\n- `Ctrl+Enter` (whenTyping:true) in LecturerView when the question form is active: invoke `previewCorrectSQL()` (NOT saveQuestion — too destructive for a keystroke).\n- `Escape` (whenTyping:false): in ConfirmDialogHost, resolve(false). Already partially present — refactor to use the composable.\n- Tab-trap inside ConfirmDialogHost: see ARCH-025 (focus trap); the composable is not used for tab trapping (handled by separate focus-trap util).\n\nNON-GOALS for this round: no global '/' search, no g+letter navigation, no per-tab shortcuts in LecturerView. Add them later.\n\nVitest plan: `frontend/src/__tests__/composables/useKeyboardShortcut.test.ts` — mount a host component, dispatch KeyboardEvent, assert handler called / not called when target is an <input>.",
