r(--color-border);\n  }\n  .nav-links button.active {\n    background-color: var(--color-primary); color: var(--color-surface);\n    border-bottom-color: var(--color-primary);\n  }\n  /* Active-route bottom border on mobile, per backlog */\n  .nav-links button.active::after { content: ''; display: block; height: 3px; background: var(--color-primary); margin-top: var(--space-2); }\n  .user-info { margin-right: 0; padding-bottom: 0.4rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }\n  .content { margin: 1.5rem auto; padding: 0 0.75rem; max-width: 100%; }\n}\n```\n- Backdrop: optional, add `<div v-if=\"navOpen\" class=\"nav-backdrop\" @click=\"navOpen=false\"/>` with `position: fixed; inset: 0; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); z-index: 99;` — mobile only.\n- Escape key (use `useKeyboardShortcut` from ARCH-021): close drawer.\n- Trap focus inside drawer when open (use `useFocusTrap` from ARCH-025) — gated to mobile (use `window.matchMedia('(max-width: 767.98px)').matches`).\n\nVitest: mount App.vue with a stub router, click hamburger, assert `aria-expanded=true` and the nav-links has `is-open` class. Navigate, assert it closes.\n\ndone_when: At <768px the hamburger appears, top-bar stays compact; clicking the hamburger slides the drawer in from the right; clicking a link navigates and auto-closes; pressing Escape closes; resizing past 768px auto-closes. Desktop layout (>=768px) unchanged.",
